          "kicker": "Rankings threat",
          "heading": "Australia could overtake England in the rankings with a Bledisloe win over All Blacks",
          "body": "England hold fifth in the World Rugby rankings on 85.68 points, only 0.79 clear of Australia in sixth on 84.89. This weekend's second Bledisloe Test in Sydney could decide whether that gap survives: a Wallabies win would take them above England into fifth, while a draw would keep them sixth. The Wallabies lost the first Test 50-19 at Eden Park, and All Blacks coach Dave Rennie's side remain second in the table behind South Africa."
