      "edition": "Saturday 17 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Travel scare",
          "heading": "France's Bielle-Biarrey stranded at Bristol Airport before Champions Cup opener",
          "body": "Bordeaux Bègles' Champions Cup opener against Gloucester nearly began with a visa problem at Bristol Airport. France winger Louis Bielle-Biarrey, loose forward Romain Gardrat and loosehead prop Matis Perchaud were among four players stranded there, unable to join the squad at its hotel near Gloucester. A club source told AFP their electronic travel authorisations were linked to passports renewed earlier this year, with no new permits obtained. The French embassy in London helped resolve it, and the group rejoined the squad."
        },
